Emit NVIDIA guest bind-mounts only for payload that is installed.

Applies on top of 0001-nvidia-integration.patch.

Upstream's 0001 emits all eleven guest bind-mounts unconditionally and
deliberately NOT 'optional', so a missing piece fails container start loudly
instead of surfacing as an opaque SurfaceFlinger crash loop. That is the right
default when the full payload ships.

At upstream v0.1.0 the ANGLE libraries and the patched surfaceflinger are not
distributed in any release or CI artifact (both are built on the maintainer's
self-hosted runner), so those mounts would fail every container start. Emit a
mount only for files actually installed under nv/guest; files that ARE present
still mount strictly, preserving upstream's fail-loudly behaviour for a
genuinely broken install.

Absent payload is logged at container start so the degradation is visible
rather than silent. Once ANGLE is built and installed, its mounts appear
again with no further change.

--- a/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -149,10 +149,18 @@ def generate_nodes_lxc_config(args):
                 "vendor/lib64/libgbm_mesa_wrapper.so",
                 "vendor/lib64/hw/hwcomposer.waydroid.so",
                 "system/bin/surfaceflinger",
             )
             for guest_file in guest_files:
+                if not os.path.exists(os.path.join(guest_root, guest_file)):
+                    # Not installed (e.g. ANGLE / patched surfaceflinger are
+                    # not distributed prebuilt upstream) - skip rather than
+                    # fail container start on a mount with no source.
+                    logging.info(
+                        "waydroid-nvidia: guest payload not installed, "
+                        "skipping bind-mount: {}".format(guest_file))
+                    continue
                 nodes.append(
                     "lxc.mount.entry = {}/{} {} none rbind,create=file 0 0".format(
                         guest_root, guest_file, guest_file))
         else:
             # Compatibility with installations provisioned before the dual-ABI
